    "scope": "Passive record-field contracts and lexical reference constraints only. No graph closure, payload hash verification, document rendering, successful verification or write authorization. 10.b.W builds an owned inert BaselineManifest for working/release labels over explicitly resolved unconfigured scopes. The existing fingerprint_scope function supplies the exact precreation Scope-Hash and model root. Every selected artifact, profile, rule, mapping and attachment is retained as canonical JSON or exact raw SnapshotObject bytes; missing, surplus, stale and mismatched inputs fail. The manifest includes schema/tool versions, ordered active profile identities and hashes, the effective supplied semantic configuration snapshot/hash, recomposed effective-profile bytes, boundary references and complete object rows with role, identity/version/revision, relative source path, length, media type, hash and archive path. Identical bytes deduplicate across roles. Tests bind independent actual digests, the existing model-root contract, external-store round trips, owned values and isolated Core/PYZ behavior. Complete live-project/provider validation, configured/language/archival integration, Baseline artifact creation, journal publication and release readiness are outside this W preparation; no full-suite or release success is claimed. 10.b.R rebuilds scope inventory and dependency observations from owned original artifact bytes and validated resource/attachment values before accepting closure. Stale identities, relation caches, active flags and inventory/dependency fingerprints are rejected. An optional planned baseline_id must be a project Baseline identity absent from the entire source inventory, including unselected controls; it is retained outside the precreation model root. The later writer must supply that identity. Regression cases show that local roots/inodes, runtime clocks/timezones, display/generated-path settings and soft operational limits do not affect portable model bytes, whereas normative artifact audit bytes still affect the root. Resource paths, exact mappings, actual profile recomposition and missing/stale boundaries fail conservatively. The original W tests and limited provider/publication scope remain unchanged. 10.b.C moves unchanged original-byte inventory/profile/payload admission into archive._baseline_inputs. BaselineManifest and the assembler retain their exact function/class bodies and continue to call the existing graph.scope_hash.fingerprint_scope; no second semantic hash implementation is introduced. All W/R test files and behavior expectations remain byte-identical."
  },
